{
  "title": "52: At-Tur الطور",
  "data": "بِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمٰنِ الرَّحِيْمِ\nBISMIL LAAHIR RAHMAANIR RAHEEM\nIn the Name of Allah, the All-beneficent, the All-merciful\nوَالطُّوْرِۙ‏(1)\nWAT TOOR.\nBy the Mount [Sinai],\nوَكِتٰبٍ مَّسْطُوْرٍۙ‏(2)\nWA KETAABIM MASTOOR.\nby the Book inscribed\nفِىْ رَقٍّ مَّنْشُوْرٍۙ‏(3)\nFEE RAQQIM MANSHOOR.\non an unrolled parchment;\nوَالْبَيْتِ الْمَعْمُوْرِۙ‏(4)\nWAL BAYTIL MA’MOOR.\nby the House greatly frequented;\nوَالسَّقْفِ الْمَرْفُوْعِۙ‏(5)\nWAS SAQFIL MARFOO’.\nby the vault raised high,\nوَالْبَحْرِ الْمَسْجُوْرِۙ‏(6)\nWAL BAHRIL MASJOOR.\nby the surging sea:\nاِنَّ عَذَابَ رَبِّكَ لوَاقِعٌ ۙ‏(7)\nINNA A’ZAABA RABBEKA LA-WAAQE’.\nindeed your Lord’s punishment will surely befall.\nمَّا لَهٗ مِنْ دَافِعٍۙ‏(8)\nMAA LAHU MIN DAAFE’.\nThere is none who can avert it.\nيَّوْمَ تَمُوْرُ السَّمَآءُ مَوْرًا ۙ‏(9)\nYAWMA TAMOORUS SAMAAA-O MAWRAA.\nOn the day when the sky whirls violently,\nوَّتَسِيْرُ الْجِبَالُ سَيْرًا ؕ‏(10)\nWA TASEERUL JEBAALO SAYRAA.\nand the mountains move with an awful motion:\nفَوَيْلٌ يَّوْمَئِذٍ لِّلْمُكَذِّبِيْنَۙ‏(11)\nFA-WAYLUN-Y YAWMA-EZIL LIL-MOKAZZEBEEN.\nwoe to the deniers on that day\nالَّذِيْنَ هُمْ فِىْ خَوْضٍ يَّلْعَبُوْنَۘ‏(12)\nLAZEENA HUM FEE KHAWZIN-Y YAL-A’BOON.\n—those who play around in vain talk,\nيَوْمَ يُدَعُّوْنَ اِلٰى نَارِ جَهَنَّمَ دَعًّاؕ‏(13)\nYAWMA YODA’-O’ONA ELAA NAARE JAHANNAMA DA’-A’A.\nthe day when they will be shoved forcibly toward the fire of hell, [and told:]\nهٰذِهِ النَّارُ الَّتِىْ كُنْتُمْ بِهَا تُكَذِّبُوْنَ‏(14)\nHAAZEHIN NAARUL LATEE KUNTUM BEHAA TOKAZZEBOON.\n‘This is the Fire which you used to deny!\nاَفَسِحْرٌ هٰذَاۤ اَمْ اَنْتُمْ لَا تُبْصِرُوْنَۚ‏(15)\nAFA-SEHRUN HAAZAA AM ANTUM LAA TUBSEROON.\nIs this, then, [also] magic, or is it you who do not perceive?\nاِصْلَوْهَا فَاصْبِرُوْۤا اَوْ لَا تَصْبِرُوْاۚ سَوَآءٌ عَلَيْكُمْؕ اِنَّمَا تُجْزَوْنَ مَا كُنْتُمْ تَعْمَلُوْنَ‏(16)\nISLAWHAA FASBEROO AW LAA TASBEROO, SAWAAA-UN A’LAYKUM, INNAMAA TUJZAWNA MAA KUNTUM TA’MALOON.\nEnter it, and it will be the same for you whether you are patient or impatient. You are only being requited for what you used to do.’\nاِنَّ الْمُتَّقِيْنَ فِىْ جَنّٰتٍ وَّنَعِيْمٍۙ‏(17)\nINNAL MUTTAQEENA FEE JANNAATINW WA NA-E’EM.\nIndeed the Godwary will be amid gardens and bliss,\nفٰكِهِيْنَ بِمَاۤ اٰتٰٮهُمْ رَبُّهُمْۚ وَوَقٰٮهُمْ رَبُّهُمْ عَذَابَ الْجَحِيْمِ‏(18)\nFAAKEHEENA BEMAA AATAAHUM RABBOHUM, WA WAQAAHUM RABBOHUM A’ZAABAL JAHEEM.\nrejoicing because of what their Lord has given them, and that their Lord has saved them from the punishment of hell.\nكُلُوْا وَاشْرَبُوْا هَنِٓيْئًا ۢ بِمَا كُنْتُمْ تَعْمَلُوْنَۙ‏(19)\nKOLOO WASH RABOO HANEE-AM BEMAA KUNTUM TA’MALOON.\n[They will be told:] ‘Enjoy your food and drink, [as a reward] for what you used to do.’\nمُتَّكِئِيْنَ عَلٰى سُرُرٍ مَّصْفُوْفَةٍ ۚ وَزَوَّجْنٰهُمْ بِحُوْرٍ عِيْنٍ‏(20)\nMUTTAKE-EENA A’LAA SORORIM MASFOOFAH, WA ZAWWAJNAAHUM BE-HOORIN E’EN.\nThey will be reclining on arrayed couches, and We will wed them to big-eyed houris.\nوَالَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا وَاتَّبَعَتْهُمْ ذُرِّيَّتُهُمْ بِاِيْمَانٍ اَلْحَقْنَا بِهِمْ ذُرِّيَّتَهُمْ وَمَاۤ اَلَتْنٰهُمْ مِّنْ عَمَلِهِمْ مِّنْ شَىْءٍؕ كُلُّ امْرِیءٍۢ بِمَا كَسَبَ رَهِيْنٌ‏(21)\nWAL LAZEENA AAMANOO WAT TABA-A’THUM ZURRIYYATOHUM BE-EEMAANIN ALHAQNAA BEHIM ZURRIYYATAHUM WA MAA ALATNAAHUM MIN A’MALEHIM MIN SHAY, KULLUM RE-IM BEMAA KASABA RAHEEN.\nThe faithful and their descendants who followed them in faith—We will make their descendants join them, and We will not stint anything from [the reward of] their deeds. Every person is hostage to what he has earned.\nوَاَمْدَدْنٰهُمْ بِفَاكِهَةٍ وَّلَحْمٍ مِّمَّا يَشْتَهُوْنَ‏(22)\nWA AMDADNAAHUM BE-FAAKEHATINW WA LAHMIM MIMMAA YASHTAHOON.\nWe will provide them with fruits and meat, such as they desire.\nيَتَنَازَعُوْنَ فِيْهَا كَاْسًا لَّا لَغْوٌ فِيْهَا وَلَا تَاْثِيْمٌ‏(23)\nYATANAAZA-O’ONA FEEHAA KAASAL LAA LAGHWUN FEEHAA WA LAA TAASEEM.\nThere they will pass from hand to hand a cup wherein there will be neither any vain talk nor sinful speech.\nوَيَطُوْفُ عَلَيْهِمْ غِلْمَانٌ لَّهُمْ كَاَنَّهُمْ لُؤْلُؤٌ مَّكْنُوْنٌ‏(24)\nWA YATOOFO A’LAYHIM GHILMAANUL LAHUM KA-ANNAHUM LOALO-UM MAKNOON.\nThey will be waited upon by their youths, as if they were guarded pearls.\nوَاَقْبَلَ بَعْضُهُمْ عَلٰى بَعْضٍ يَّتَسَآءَلُوْنَ‏(25)\nWA AQBALA BA’ZOHUM A’LAA BA’ZIN-Y YATASAAA-ALOON.\nThey will turn to one another, questioning each other.\nقَالُوْۤا اِنَّا كُنَّا قَبْلُ فِىْۤ اَهْلِنَا مُشْفِقِيْنَ‏(26)\nQAALOO INNAA KUNNAA QABLO FEE AHLENAA MUSHFEQEEN.\nThey will say, ‘Indeed, aforetime, we used to be apprehensive about our families.\nفَمَنَّ اللّٰهُ عَلَيْنَا وَوَقٰٮنَا عَذَابَ السَّمُوْمِ‏(27)\nFA-MANNAL LAAHO A’LAYNAA WA WAQAANAA A’ZAABAS SAMOOM.\nBut Allah showed us favour and He saved us from the punishment of the [infernal] miasma.\nاِنَّا كُنَّا مِنْ قَبْلُ نَدْعُوْهُ ؕ اِنَّهٗ هُوَ الْبَرُّ الرَّحِيْمُ‏(28)\nINNAA KUNNAA MIN QABLO NAD-O’OH, INNAHU HOWAL BARRUR RAHEEM.\nWe used to supplicate Him aforetime. Indeed He is the All-benign, the All-merciful.’\nفَذَكِّرْ فَمَاۤ اَنْتَ بِنِعْمَتِ رَبِّكَ بِكَاهِنٍ وَّلَا مَجْنُوْنٍؕ‏(29)\nFA-ZAKKIR FAMAA ANTA BE-NE’MATE RABBEKA BE-KAAHENINW WA LAA MAJNOON.\nSo admonish. By your Lord’s blessing, you are not a soothsayer, nor mad.\nاَمْ يَقُوْلُوْنَ شَاعِرٌ نَّتَرَبَّصُ بِهٖ رَيْبَ الْمَنُوْنِ‏(30)\nAM YAQOOLOONA SHAA-E’RUN NATARABBASO BEHI RAYBAL MANOON.\nDo they say, ‘[He is] a poet, for whom we await a fatal accident’?\nقُلْ تَرَبَّصُوْا فَاِنِّىْ مَعَكُمْ مِّنَ الْمُتَرَبِّصِيْنَ ؕ‏(31)\nQUL TARABBASOO FA-INNEE MA-A’KUM MENAL MOTARABBESEEN.\nSay, ‘Wait! I too am waiting along with you.’\nاَمْ تَاْمُرُهُمْ اَحْلَامُهُمْ بِهٰذَآ اَمْ هُمْ قَوْمٌ طَاغُوْنَۚ‏(32)\nAM TAAMOROHUM AHLAAMOHUM BEHAAZAA AM HUM QAWMUN TAAGHOON.\nIs it their intellect which prompts them to [say] this, or are they a rebellious lot?\nاَمْ يَقُوْلُوْنَ تَقَوَّلَهٗ ۚ بَلْ لَّا يُؤْمِنُوْنَ ۚ‏(33)\nAM YAQOOLOONA TAQAWWALAH, BAL LAA YOAMENOON.\nDo they say, ‘He has improvised it [himself]?’ Rather, they have no faith!\nفَلْيَاْتُوْا بِحَدِيْثٍ مِّثْلِهٖۤ اِنْ كَانُوْا صٰدِقِيْنَؕ‏(34)\nFALYAATOO BE-HADEESIM MISLEHI IN KAANOO SAADEQEEN.\nLet them bring a discourse like it, if they are truthful.\nاَمْ خُلِقُوْا مِنْ غَيْرِ شَىْءٍ اَمْ هُمُ الْخٰلِقُوْنَؕ‏(35)\nAM KHOLEQOO MIN GHAYRE SHAY-IN AM HOMUL KHAALEQOON.\nWere they created from nothing? Or are they [their own] creators?\nاَمْ خَلَقُوا السَّمٰوٰتِ وَالْاَرْضَۚ بَلْ لَّا يُوْقِنُوْنَؕ‏(36)\nAM KHALAQUS SAMAAWAATE WAL ARZ, BAL LAA YOOQENOON.\nDid they create the heavens and the earth? Rather, they have no certainty!\nاَمْ عِنْدَهُمْ خَزَآئِنُ رَبِّكَ اَمْ هُمُ الْمُصَۜيْطِرُوْنَؕ‏(37)\nAM I’NDAHUM KHAZAAA-ENO RABBEKA AM HOMUL MOSAYTEROON.\nDo they possess the treasuries of your Lord? Or do they control [them]?\nاَمْ لَهُمْ سُلَّمٌ يَّسْتَمِعُوْنَ فِيْهِ ۚ فَلْيَاْتِ مُسْتَمِعُهُمْ بِسُلْطٰنٍ مُّبِيْنٍؕ‏(38)\nAM LAHUM SULLAMUN-Y YASTAME-O’ONA FEEH, FALYAATE MUSTAME-O’HUM BE-SULTAANIM MOBEEN.\nDo they have a ladder [leading up to heaven] whereby they eavesdrop? If so, let their eavesdropper produce a manifest authority.\nاَمْ لَهُ الْبَنٰتُ وَلَكُمُ الْبَنُوْنَؕ‏(39)\nAM LAHUL BANAATO WA LAKOMUL BANOON.\nDoes He have daughters while you have sons?\nاَمْ تَسْئَلُهُمْ اَجْرًا فَهُمْ مِّنْ مَّغْرَمٍ مُّثْقَلُوْنَؕ‏(40)\nAM TAS-ALOHUM AJRAN FAHUM MIM MAGHRAMIM MUSQALOON.\nDo you ask them for a reward, so that they are [wary of] being weighed down with debt?\nاَمْ عِنْدَهُمُ الْغَيْبُ فَهُمْ يَكْتُبُوْنَؕ‏(41)\nAM I’NDAHOMUL GHAYBO FAHUM YAKTOBOON.\nDo they have [access to] the Unseen, which they write down?\nاَمْ يُرِيْدُوْنَ كَيْدًاؕ فَالَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْا هُمُ الْمَكِيْدُوْنَؕ‏(42)\nAM YOREEDOONA KAYDAA, FALLAZEENA KAFAROO HOMUL MAKEEDOON.\nDo they seek to outmaneuver [Allah]? But it is the faithless who are the outmaneuvered ones!\nاَمْ لَهُمْ اِلٰهٌ غَيْرُ اللّٰهِؕ سُبْحٰنَ اللّٰهِ عَمَّا يُشْرِكُوْنَ‏(43)\nAM LAHUM ELAAHUN GHAYRUL LAAH, SUBHAANAL LAAHE A’MMAA YUSHREKOON.\nDo they have any god other than Allah? Clear is Allah of any partners that they may ascribe [to Him]!\nوَاِنْ يَّرَوْا كِسْفًا مِّنَ السَّمَآءِ سَاقِطًا يَّقُوْلُوْا سَحَابٌ مَّرْكُوْمٌ‏(44)\nWA IN-Y YARAW KISFAM MENAS SAMAAA-E SAAQETAN-Y YAQOOLOO SAHAABUM MARKOOM.\nWere they to see a fragment falling from the sky, they would say, ‘A cumulous cloud.’\nفَذَرْهُمْ حَتّٰى يُلٰقُوْا يَوْمَهُمُ الَّذِىْ فِيْهِ يُصْعَقُوْنَۙ‏(45)\nFA-ZARHUM HATTAA YOLAAQOO YAWMAHOMUL LAZEE FEEHE YUS-A’QOON.\nSo leave them until they encounter the day when they will be thunderstruck,\nيَوْمَ لَا يُغْنِىْ عَنْهُمْ كَيْدُهُمْ شَيْئًا وَّلَا هُمْ يُنْصَرُوْنَؕ‏(46)\nYAWMA LAA YUGHNEE A’NHUM KAYDOHUM SHAY-ANW WA LAA HUM YUNSAROON.\nthe day when their guile will not avail them in any way, nor will they be helped.\nوَاِنَّ لِلَّذِيْنَ ظَلَمُوْا عَذَابًا دُوْنَ ذٰلِكَ وَلٰكِنَّ اَكْثَرَهُمْ لَا يَعْلَمُوْنَ‏(47)\nWA INNA LILLAZEENA ZALAMOO A’ZAABAN DOONA ZAALEKA WA LAAKINNA AKSARAHUM LAA YA’LAMOON.\nIndeed there is a punishment besides that for those who do wrong, but most of them do not know.\nوَاصْبِرْ لِحُكْمِ رَبِّكَ فَاِنَّكَ بِاَعْيُنِنَا وَسَبِّحْ بِحَمْدِ رَبِّكَ حِيْنَ تَقُوْمُۙ‏(48)\nWAS BIR LE-HUKME RABBEKA FA-INNAKA BE-A-A’YONENAA WA SABBEH BE-HAMDE RABBEKA HEENA TAQOOM.\nSo submit patiently to the judgement of your Lord, for indeed you fare before Our eyes. And celebrate the praise of your Lord when you rise [at dawn],\nوَمِنَ الَّيْلِ فَسَبِّحْهُ وَاِدْبَارَ النُّجُوْمِ‏(49)\nWA MENAL LAYLE FA-SABBEHHO WA IDBAARAN NOJOOM.\nand also glorify Him during the night and at the receding of the stars.",
  "merits": "Surah al-Toor (The Mountain)\nThis Surah has 49 verses and it was revealed in Makkah. The Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.) said that the one who recites this Surah will be kept safe from the wrath and punishment of Allah (s.w.t.).\nImam Ja’far al-Sadiq (a.s.) has said that the recitation of this Surah brings good fortune to the reciter and constant recitation by those who have been imprisoned secures an early release from bondage. Surah al-Toor, if recited or kept as a talisman, keeps children in good health."
}
